astrobench_f31aa696a1,astrobench_f31aa696a1_chunk_036,36,"Forward-modelling Milky Way Cepheids: selection effects and physical priors in the Gaia-HST calibration 3.3 Likelihoods For each MW Cepheid, the observed Wesenheit magnitude andGaiaEDR3 parallax are compared to their predicted values. The magnitude likelihood for theithCepheid, con- ditioned on the true periodlogP iand metallicity[O/H] i, is L(mW H,obs,i |di,logP i,[O/H] i,Λ)",3.3 Likelihoods,3.3 Likelihoods,,,,,Forward-modelling Milky Way Cepheids: selection effects and physical priors in the Gaia-HST calibration,"Richard Stiskalek, Adam Riess, Harry Desmond, Guilhem Lavaux, Dan Scolnic",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-10T16:39:31Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.09880v1,2603.09880,distribution_functions,67,51,False,False,0,51
astrobench_f31aa696a1,astrobench_f31aa696a1_chunk_037,37,"Forward-modelling Milky Way Cepheids: selection effects and physical priors in the Gaia-HST calibration =N mW H,obs,i |mW H,pred,i ,q σ2 m,i+ (σci int)2 ,(12) whereσ m,iis the photometric uncertainty andσci intthe in- trinsic scatter for campaignc i∈ {C22,C27}. The parallax likelihood is L(ϖ obs,i|di,Λ) =N(ϖ obs,i|ϖpred,i, σϖ,i),(13) whereσ ϖ,iis the reportedGaiaparallax uncertainty. The period measurement uncertainties are negligibly small, so the period likelihood is effectively a delta function, L(logP obs,i|logP i)≈δ(logP obs,i−logP i).(14) For the metallicity, individual measurement uncertainties are rarely reported; the dominant errors are methodological and approximately constant across the sample. We there- fore adopt a Gaussian likelihood with a fixed measure- ment uncertaintyϵ [O/H] = 0.06 dex, consistent with the ∼0.05 dexsystematic scale uncertainty adopted by Gieren et al. (2018), the∼0.07 dexpropagated measurement er- ror reported by Romaniello et al. (2022), and the≲0.05 dex precision achieved in the homogeneous reanalysis of da Silva et al. (2022). The exact value has negligible impact on the inference, as it enters only through the precision-weighted combination with the population scatterσ [O/H]. L([O/H] obs,i|[O/H] i) =N([O/H] obs,i|[O/H] i, ϵ[O/H]), (15) whereϵ",=N,=N,,,,,Forward-modelling Milky Way Cepheids: selection effects and physical priors in the Gaia-HST calibration,"Richard Stiskalek, Adam Riess, Harry Desmond, Guilhem Lavaux, Dan Scolnic",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-10T16:39:31Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.09880v1,2603.09880,distribution_functions,234,180,False,True,0,180
