astrobench_a877243f10,astrobench_a877243f10_chunk_057,57,"Distribution functions for spheroids APPENDIX A: LIMITING FORM OF ∂JR/∂VT Here we infer the limit as vt→0 of equation (9). ∂Jr ∂vt/vextendsingle/vextendsingle/vextendsingle/vextendsingle r=vt π/integraldisplayra rpdr′1−r2/r′2 /radicalbig 2(E−Φ)−L2/r′2. (A1) Since the second term in the numerator dominates as rp tends tozero, we retain only this term. We extract afactor L from the denominator and r2from the surviving numerator and change integration variable from r′tou≡1/r′. Then we have ∂Jr ∂vt/vextendsingle/vextendsingle/vextendsingle/vextendsingle r≃ −sgn(vt)r π/integraldisplayup uadu√ a2−u2, (A2) where a2= 2E−Φ(r′)",APPENDIX A: LIMITING FORM OF ∂JR/∂VT,APPENDIX A: LIMITING FORM OF ∂JR/∂VT,,,,,Distribution functions for spheroids,James Binney,astro-ph.GA,2026-02-26T15:41:51Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2602.23127v1,2602.23127,distribution_functions,101,77,False,True,0,77
