astrobench_79edfd6850,astrobench_79edfd6850_chunk_048,48,"Constraining the Galactic bar and spiral pattern speeds with the Hyades tidal stream 4. DISCUSSION AND LIMIT A TIONS Our comparison of the simulated and observed stream morphology and density structure favors models with Ωb≃40–45 km s−1kpc−1and Ωs= 22.5 km s−1kpc−1; here we discuss limitations and potential systematics af- fecting this inference. A striking feature of the observed Gaia data is the pro- nounced asymmetry between the two tidal tails, with one side appearing significantly more populated than the other. In contrast, while our simulated models un- der the influence of the bar and spiral arms do exhibit some degree of asymmetry , they do not fully reproduce the near-disappearance of one tail seen in the observa- tions. A possible explanation is that the high level of 11 4 3 2 1 01234v,sim(kms1) No spiral arms, b = 37.5km/s No spiral arms, b = 40km/s No spiral arms, b = 42.5km/s No spiral arms, b = 45km/s 4 3 2 1 01234v,sim(kms1) b = 37.5km/s, s = 22.5km/s b = 40km/s, s = 22.5km/s b = 42.5km/s, s = 22.5km/s",4. DISCUSSION AND LIMIT A TIONS,4. DISCUSSION AND LIMIT A TIONS,,,,,Constraining the Galactic bar and spiral pattern speeds with the Hyades tidal stream,"Zi-yi Zhou, Long Wang, Tereza Jerabkova, Zhenghao He",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-31T07:33:52Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.29360v1,2603.29360,galactic_dynamics,234,180,False,True,0,180
