astrobench_79edfd6850,astrobench_79edfd6850_chunk_053,53,"0.4 0.2 0.0 0.2 0.4 Xrot [kpc] Figure 11. In each subplot, Upper panel: Spatial distribution of the model (grey points) and the corresponding selected final members (red points). Both the model and final members are shown in the stream-aligned coordinate system (Xrot, Yrot), where thexrot -axis is aligned with the principal direction of the stream’s elongation. Lower panel: Comparison of the longitudinal density distribution along the stream for the model (grey lines) and the final members (red histogram). may undergo secular evolution, meaning their pattern speeds could be time-dependent ( T. Hilmi et al. 2020 ). By adopting a static bar geometry and Ωb, our model might slightly shift the exact resonance positions, which could influence the predicted stream morphology . In addition, the intrinsic parameters of the Hyades cluster, specifically its age and initial mass, also intro- duce uncertainties. While we adopted an age of 648 Myr and an initial mass of 800M⊙based on recent literature (L. W ang & T. Jerabkova 2021 ), different age estimates ranging from 600 to800 Myr (e.g., M. A. C. Perryman et",4. DISCUSSION AND LIMIT A TIONS,4. DISCUSSION AND LIMIT A TIONS,,,,,Constraining the Galactic bar and spiral pattern speeds with the Hyades tidal stream,"Zi-yi Zhou, Long Wang, Tereza Jerabkova, Zhenghao He",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-31T07:33:52Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.29360v1,2603.29360,galactic_dynamics,234,180,False,False,700,880
astrobench_79edfd6850,astrobench_79edfd6850_chunk_054,54,"uncertainties. While we adopted an age of 648 Myr and an initial mass of 800M⊙based on recent literature (L. W ang & T. Jerabkova 2021 ), different age estimates ranging from 600 to800 Myr (e.g., M. A. C. Perryman et al. 1998 ;S. De Gennaro et al. 2009 ;S. Reino et al. 2018 ;Gaia Collaboration et al. 2018 ) would directly af- fect the simulated length of the tidal tails. Similarly , the exact solar position ( R0) and velocity ( v⊙) are still sub-jects of refinement. Since the transformation from ICRS to Galactocentric coordinates is highly sensitive to these solar parameters, small variations in (R0, V⊙)could lead to systematic shifts in the estimated orbit of the Hyades (M. J. Reid et al. 2019 ;GRA VITY Collaboration et al. 2022 ). F urthermore, determining the precise initial phase- space coordinates of the cluster 648 Myr ago remains a challenge. Although we utilized the Nelder-Mead op- timization method to refine the backward-integrated or- bit, the chaotic nature of orbits in a non-axisymmetric potential means that the “initial guess” may not be",4. DISCUSSION AND LIMIT A TIONS,4. DISCUSSION AND LIMIT A TIONS,,,,,Constraining the Galactic bar and spiral pattern speeds with the Hyades tidal stream,"Zi-yi Zhou, Long Wang, Tereza Jerabkova, Zhenghao He",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-31T07:33:52Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.29360v1,2603.29360,galactic_dynamics,234,180,False,False,840,1020
astrobench_79edfd6850,astrobench_79edfd6850_chunk_055,55,"of the cluster 648 Myr ago remains a challenge. Although we utilized the Nelder-Mead op- timization method to refine the backward-integrated or- bit, the chaotic nature of orbits in a non-axisymmetric potential means that the “initial guess” may not be unique. The resulting trajectory is a best-fit solution, but the sensitivity of the tidal tail formation to the ex- 13 act orbital path suggests that these initial conditions remain a significant source of uncertainty .",4. DISCUSSION AND LIMIT A TIONS,4. DISCUSSION AND LIMIT A TIONS,,,,,Constraining the Galactic bar and spiral pattern speeds with the Hyades tidal stream,"Zi-yi Zhou, Long Wang, Tereza Jerabkova, Zhenghao He",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-31T07:33:52Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.29360v1,2603.29360,galactic_dynamics,98,75,False,False,980,1055
astrobench_79edfd6850,astrobench_79edfd6850_chunk_056,56,"Constraining the Galactic bar and spiral pattern speeds with the Hyades tidal stream 5. CONCLUSIONS W e modeled the formation of the Hyades tidal stream with direct N-body simulations ( PETAR ) in a multi- component Milky W ay potential implemented with AGAMA and including a rotating bar and spiral arms. By systematically varying the bar and spiral pattern speeds, we quantified how non-axisymmetric forcing re- shapes the stream orientation, length, and internal den- sity structure over the ∼648 Myr evolution of the clus- ter. W e then confronted the models with observations by combining CP/CCP-based kinematic selection on Gaia EDR3 with an adaptive three-dimensional spatial matching technique. The key observational constraint is the stream-aligned longitudinal density profile of the Gaia candidates. This profile shows a prominent peak at Yrot≈0.1 kpc , which is consistent with the overdensity reported by T. Jer- abkova et al. (2021 ). W e find that this feature is best reproduced by models with Ωs= 22.5 km s−1kpc−1and Ωb≃40–45 km s−1kpc−1, supporting a relatively slow Galactic bar. These findings also indicate that the in- clusion",5. CONCLUSIONS,5. CONCLUSIONS,,,,,Constraining the Galactic bar and spiral pattern speeds with the Hyades tidal stream,"Zi-yi Zhou, Long Wang, Tereza Jerabkova, Zhenghao He",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-31T07:33:52Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.29360v1,2603.29360,galactic_dynamics,234,180,False,True,0,180
astrobench_79edfd6850,astrobench_79edfd6850_chunk_057,57,"T. Jer- abkova et al. (2021 ). W e find that this feature is best reproduced by models with Ωs= 22.5 km s−1kpc−1and Ωb≃40–45 km s−1kpc−1, supporting a relatively slow Galactic bar. These findings also indicate that the in- clusion of spiral arms is not negligible and Ωsaround this intermediate value are favored. More broadly , our results demonstrate that nearby open-cluster streams provide a complementary , local avenue to constrain non-axisymmetric Galactic dynamics using not only the global stream orientation but also its fine-grained den- sity structure.ACKNOWLEDGMENTS L W thanks the support from the National Natural Science F oundation of China through grant 12573041 and 12233013, the High-level Y outh T alent Project (Provincial Financial Allocation) through the grant 2023HYSPT0706, the F undamental Research F unds for the Central Universities, Sun Y at-sen Univer- sity (2025QNPY04). TJ acknowledges the support from the MUNI A ward in Science and Humanities",5. CONCLUSIONS,5. CONCLUSIONS,,,,,Constraining the Galactic bar and spiral pattern speeds with the Hyades tidal stream,"Zi-yi Zhou, Long Wang, Tereza Jerabkova, Zhenghao He",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-31T07:33:52Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.29360v1,2603.29360,galactic_dynamics,195,150,False,True,140,290
