astrobench_1e3dee4300,astrobench_1e3dee4300_chunk_037,37,"Bar Properties and Star-by-Star Bar Membership via Action Conservation 4 STAR-BY-STAR CLASSIFICATION The benefit of using the conservation of action to classify the bar is that the actions must be first calculated on a star-by-star basis. This means that it is possible to identify whether a given star particle in the simulation is likely to be on a bar orbit, helping us to exclude starparticleswhichmaysimplybepassingthroughtheidentifiedbar region. This kind of star-by-star classification could then allow for more precise studies of the stellar populations or properties of the bar,ratherthansimplyofbar-locatedstellarpopulationsorproperties. AnexampleofthisispresentedinFigure6.Inthisfigure,thestellar massdensityisagainprojectededge-on(𝑥𝑧-upper)andface-on(𝑥𝑦",4 STAR-BY-STAR CLASSIFICATION,4 STAR-BY-STAR CLASSIFICATION,,,,,Bar Properties and Star-by-Star Bar Membership via Action Conservation,"Elizabeth J. Iles, Finn A. Pal, Joss Bland-Hawthorn, Ken Freeman",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-26T02:45:29Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.24952v1,2603.24952,galactic_dynamics,116,89,False,False,0,89
