astrobench_b7b4f9944a,astrobench_b7b4f9944a_chunk_053,53,"Quantifying the Milky Way, LMC and their interaction using all-sky kinematics of outer halo stars 6.2 Caveats and Limitations OurapproachofusingrigidmodelsfortheMW–LMCsystemscomes with various caveats. Some of the limitations of rigid models in- clude: assuming that the MW is in equilibrium prior the LMC’s infall (e.g., Deason et al. 2017), assuming there is no mass lost or gained by either halo, not accounting for halo triaxiality, and usingasimpleChandrasekharprescriptionfordynamicalfriction(seedis- cussionsectionsinBrooksetal.2026,2025).Ideally,onewouldusea suiteof𝑁-bodyMW–LMCsimulationsthatcannaturallyaccountfor most of the above limitations. Moreover,𝑁-body simulations would allowtheMWdisctomoveseparatelyfromitsdarkmatterhalo,bet- termodellingtheinducedreflexmotionfromtheLMC(Yaaqibetal.",6.2 Caveats and Limitations,6.2 Caveats and Limitations,,,,,"Quantifying the Milky Way, LMC and their interaction using all-sky kinematics of outer halo stars","Richard A. N. Brooks, Jason L. Sanders, Adam M. Dillamore, Nicolás Garavito-Camargo, Vedant Chandra, Adrian M. Price-Whelan, Phillip Cargile",astro-ph.GA,2026-03-09T18:00:04Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.08788v1,2603.08788,galactic_dynamics,102,78,False,False,0,78
