astrobench_c59a82f3b2,astrobench_c59a82f3b2_chunk_018,18,"Comparing dynamical effects of the central bar and the spiral arms in the solar neighborhood R, (2) with the boundary condition lim R→∞Φ0(R) = 0. 3.2. Spiral arms potential The spiral arms model that describes the density pro- file observed in the Galaxy disk was proposed in Jun- queira et al. (2013). The 2D potential in the equatorial plane of the disk can be written as Φsp(R, φ) =−ζ0Re−g(R,φ), (3) where g(R, φ) is a function defined by g(R, φ) =R2 σ2h 1−cos␀ mφ−fm(R)i +ϵsR. (4) Here, fm(R) is a shape function that draws the spiral arms in logarithmic format as fm(R) =m tan(i)lnR Ri +γsp. (5) The values of the parameters in Eqs. 3–5 are listed in Table 2 and their choice is discussed in Sect. 4.1. 3.3. Central bar potential In this work, the central bar with mass Mbaris modeled by layers of homogeneous concentric ellipsoids, with a rotation speed of Ω barand a phase angle γbarwith respect to the reference direction ( X-axis). The gravitational potential produced by an ellipsoid at a point P=⟨X, Y⟩ in the","R, (2)","R, (2)",,,,,Comparing dynamical effects of the central bar and the spiral arms in the solar neighborhood,"Willian Y. Nacafucasaco, Tatiana A. Michtchenko, Douglas Barros, Jacques Lépine",astro-ph.GA,2026-02-28T20:23:14Z,http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.00800v1,2603.00800,galactic_dynamics,234,180,False,True,0,180
